From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bastiaan van der Plaat <bastiaan.v.d.plaat@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add the DS startup

duke3d_nds.c switches the ARM9 to 134 MHz in DSi mode, finds the game
data in NitroFS and on the SD card, a duke3d.grp there first, shows the
progress on the touch screen console and runs the game in a thread with
its stack in main RAM. While the game loads the top screen shows the
title screen the intro ends with, read from the GRP: the background with
the Duke Nukem and 3D logos in the title palette. Settings and savegames
go to /data/duke3d/<version>/: shareware, registered or atomic, after
the size of the GRP, extra command line options can be put in
/data/duke3d/args.txt. Errors are shown on the touch screen.
